# Build-context exclusions.
#
# There was no `.dockerignore` in this repository until PHASE 15, which meant every build sent the whole
# working tree to the daemon — `node_modules/`, `.venv/`, `.next/`, `.git/`, `data/`, the coverage
# artefacts — and, worse than the wasted upload, allowed `COPY packages ./packages` (which the web image
# needs for the workspace sources) to overlay the host's installed dependencies on top of the ones the
# image resolved for itself. A `node_modules` tree built on Windows copied into a Linux image does not
# merely waste space; it replaces the correct native binaries with unusable ones. That failure mode is
# invisible on the machine that builds it and fatal on every other.
#
# The images copy what they need explicitly (`package.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`,
# `.npmrc`, `packages/*/package.json`, `apps/*/src`, `apps/api/alembic*`, `prompts/`), so nothing here
# removes anything a Dockerfile asks for.

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Installed dependencies, from any package manager, at any depth.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output and caches.
.next
**/.next
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.pytest-tmp
.pytest-p14
.tmp
coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
*.log

# Local runtime state and generated artefacts: the compose volumes supply these at run time.
data
reports/*
!reports/README.md
playwright-report
test-results
docs/assets

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
